 format(2000); // "2s"
 ```
 
+### Compound Durations
+
+`parseCompound` sums several parts into one value. Parts can be separated by spaces, commas, or nothing, and each part needs a unit.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days 4 hours'); // 187200000
+```
+
+Unlike `parse`, it never returns `NaN`. Invalid input (empty, `'abc'`, `'1h foo'`, an unknown unit) throws a `TypeError` that includes the input.
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
